      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e it might be already the case, since we have a check in first_stage_init that prevents booting non-debuggable VM with microdroid vendor partition\n\nI also thought it would be okay since we have the guard for restricting w/ debuggable VMs only. But after double-checking it, it seems this guard doesn\u0027t be applied to the protected VMs?\n\nSo I think I need an additional patch: Restricting using vendor image in protected-nondebuggable VMs.\n\nHowever, this issue is occurred even when not applying this patch, so I think enabling restriction should be managed as a separated track, regardless judging whether merging this change or not. In latest git_main, we can pass vendor image into protected-nondebuggable VMs w/o any verification of that image. For nonprotected-nondebuggable VMs, it\u0027s blocked. Shall I file a bug of it?",
