      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T12:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "BTW, if we plan to have all the plumbing (e.g. aosp/2823592) in place in Microdroid to load (and trust) the vendor partition based on a DT-provided key and merge this CL, making pvmfw pass (and therefore trust) a host-provided key, there will be a point in time where the snapshot of AOSP has this obvious way for a malicious host to inject code into the guest kernel through vendor modules, right?\n\nI must admit I haven\u0027t followed too closely the way release cycles are now working with trunk stable but, if possible, it might be wise to delay merging the current CL until we also have the verification in place, even if that means hard-coding the pubkey in pvmfw, at first (assuming that the private part isn\u0027t public i.e. we\u0027re using a non-public test key); WDYT?",
      "revId": "bca101692c8b4240335ce16bb8a5cf1af7881859",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
