      "writtenOn": "2023-11-30T02:20:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Cool, would you mind clearing this up in the TODO?\n\nWhy not? I\u0027ll leave more detailed information for that.\n\n\u003e Do you mean --protected-vm-with-firmware?\n\nI meant `--protected` in fact, but it looks same.\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/virtualizationmanager/src/crosvm.rs;l\u003d775-780\n\nThough pvmfw doesn\u0027t run for non-protected VMs, but it runs for protected-debuggable VMs. Without this patch, enabling dm-verity for non-protected VM by merging aosp/2823592 will cause breaking tests.\n- https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/tests/testapk/src/java/com/android/microdroid/test/MicrodroidTests.java;l\u003d2132\n- https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/tests/benchmark/src/java/com/android/microdroid/benchmark/MicrodroidBenchmarks.java;l\u003d264\n\nSo I thought we have 3 kinds of solutions, and the last one was what I chose when pushing this change:\n- Don\u0027t enable verification with aosp/2823592, until final solution using ABL for protected VMs is landed.\n\n- Guard the test by making assumption running on non-protected VMs only. Then enable the verification with aosp/2823592. BTW, I should make assumption someday, since ABL won\u0027t have public key of vendor image for testing obviously. However, making assumption right now would lead suspending CI for protected VM w/ vendor image.\n\n- Use the temporary solution right now by merging this change. Though it\u0027s not enough satisfied way, but merging it wouldn\u0027t decrease the level of security.",
